  "question": {
    "text": "Two carnot engines <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> are operated in series. The first one, <math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo></math> receives heat at <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and rejects to a reservoir at temperature <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> The second engine <math><mi>B</mi></math> receives heat rejected by the first engine and, in turn, rejects to a heat reservoir at <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Calculate the temperature <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> if the work outputs of the two engines are equal:"
